---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';

export const prerender = true;
---
<SiteLayout title="Terms of Service" description="Simple terms for using Alec Wantoch's website and Google OAuth client for Omamail, including account access and third-party services." noindex>
  <article aria-labelledby="terms-heading" class="mb-12">
    <h1 id="terms-heading" class="font-semibold text-2xl mb-2 tracking-tighter">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-neutral-400">Effective <time datetime="2026-11-16">November 16, 2026</time></p>
    <div class="prose leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        These terms apply to this website and the Google OAuth client I, Alec M.
        Wantoch, provide for use with Omamail. By using them, you agree to these terms.
      </p>

      <h2>What I provide</h2>
      <p>
        This website shares my work and writing. The OAuth client lets you
        authorize Omamail to connect to your Google account. Omamail is an
        independent open-source project; its software is covered by its own
        <a href="https://github.com/huacnlee/omamail">license and documentation</a>.
        Providing this client does not imply endorsement by Google or the Omamail developers.
      </p>

      <h2>Your account and choices</h2>
      <p>
        Only connect accounts you own or have permission to use. You are
        responsible for keeping your device secure and for the messages,
        calendar changes, and other actions you authorize. Do not use the
        client for spam, abuse, unlawful activity, or attempts to bypass
        Google's access restrictions.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can stop using the client at any time and revoke its access in
        your <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">Google Account permissions</a>.
        The <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> explains data handling and deletion.
      </p>

      <h2>Other services</h2>
      <p>
        Google, Omamail, and any optional AI provider you choose have their own
        terms and policies. You are responsible for following the terms that
        apply to those services. Their availability and behavior are outside my control.
      </p>

      <h2>Availability and responsibility</h2>
      <p>
        The website and OAuth client are provided as available, without
        guarantees that they will always work, stay available, or be free of
        errors. I may change or discontinue them, including access to the OAuth
        client. Keep backups of anything important to you.
      </p>
      <p>
        To the extent the law allows, I am not responsible for losses caused by
        using or being unable to use the website or client. These terms do not
        limit any rights or protections that the law does not allow you to waive.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes and questions</h2>
      <p>
        If these terms change, I will update this page and its effective date.
        For questions, contact <a href="mailto:alec@wantoch.com">alec@wantoch.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
